      "id": "tide-sig-01",
      "name": "Kell Tarn signature",
      "shortName": "Sacrifice Draw Engine",
      "displayName": "Harvest of the Fallen",
      "displayDescription": "Abandons its own followers for a steady stream of cards and resources.",
      "summary": "A survivor-sacrifice engine that converts dissolved allies into card draw, energy, and replacement figment tokens, distinguished from its nearest sibling by prioritizing card advantage and resource accumulation over the aggressive spark-scaling and interrupt removal that sibling tide-sig-02 builds toward.",
      "description": "Tide-sig-01 is a heavily character-weighted deck (84 characters, 26 events) built around a self-sustaining sacrifice loop: low-cost survivors enter play, generate value on dissolution, and leave behind figment tokens that fuel further sacrifices. The central draw engine pairs Deathwalker (\"when an allied survivor is dissolved, draw a card\"), Soulreaver (\"when a non-figment ally is dissolved, draw a card\"), and Scuttled Fortune (\"draw a card for each ally that dissolved this turn\") with Dustborn Veteran and Defiant Holdout, which materialize survivor figments whenever non-figment allies dissolve — keeping the board replenished while churning through the deck. Energy is generated throughout this loop via Nightmare Manifest (\"abandon a character: gain 1●\"), Entropy Spike (\"dissolved: gain 1● or gain 1 maximum ●\"), Volcanic Channeler (\"when an ally is dissolved, gain 1●\"), and Exiles of the Last Light (\"abandon another character: gain 1●\"), letting the dissolve-and-replace cycle compound rather than stall. The companion hand-disruption package — Lurking Dread, Dreaming Groves, Tidecaller, and Wasteland Arbitrator — taxes the opponent's options while the sacrifice engine assembles. Compared to the closely related tide-sig-02, which doubles down on spark-scaling payoffs (Cinderheart growing with each abandon, Dreadweaver converting two sacrifices into +2✦ and two cards, Together Against the Tide providing interrupt removal after abandonment), tide-sig-01 instead densifies the pure draw-and-energy reward axis, making it a resilient midrange grind deck rather than an escalating threat engine.",
      "color": "purple",
