    {
      "id": "tide-sig-02",
      "name": "Caedryn signature",
      "shortName": "Abandon Payoff",
      "displayName": "Blood for Glory",
      "displayDescription": "Feeds on its own losses, growing strength and clearing threats with every sacrifice.",
      "summary": "A sacrifice-driven deck that converts repeated abandonment into ✦ scaling, card draw on dissolution, and interrupt removal — distinct from its nearest sibling by centering on abandonment as an active resource that fuels both challenge threat and board control, rather than hand disruption or void-size payoffs.",
      "description": "Tide-sig-02 is a heavily character-weighted deck (87 of 110 copies) built around the act of abandoning allies as the primary resource. A dense core of 2x cards establishes two interlocking loops: low-cost survivors such as Harvester of Despair and Cinderheart grow their ✦ each time a character is abandoned, turning a stream of cheap sacrifices into a board of mounting threats, while dissolution payoffs — Soulreaver drawing a card when a non-figment ally dissolves, Deathwalker doing the same for survivors, and Scuttled Fortune cashing in an entire turn of deaths — ensure that spending characters translates directly into card advantage. Volcanic Channeler and Nightmare Manifest convert dissolution and abandonment into energy (●), keeping the engine solvent. Dustborn Veteran and Defiant Holdout supply fresh survivor figments whenever the cycle consumes real characters, and low-cost recursion via Veil of the Wastes and Duskwall Delver restocks the sacrifice pile from the void. The 2x copies of Together Against the Tide — an interrupt that dissolves a ≤3● cost enemy on the same turn you abandon — give the deck reactive board control that activates naturally within the gameplan. Compared to its nearest sibling tide-sig-01, which leans toward disrupting the opponent's hand with cards like Lurking Dread and reaches for mass void recursion with Wake the Fallen, tide-sig-02 is more internally focused: it earns its advantages by treating each sacrifice as both a challenge investment (✦ growth) and a card-draw trigger, and it answers enemy threats through interrupt events unlocked by abandonment rather than stripping opponent resources from hand.",
      "color": "orange",
      "claims": {"tribe": "Survivor", "mechanics": ["abandon","figment"]},
      "role": "signature",
      "dreamAvatarId": "9D64A4A2-3DC7-456E-9EB2-5FE3A48883C4",
      "cards": [
        {"id":"0458658d-7e02-4286-9249-93674d16620b","name":"Iron Pharaoh","subtype":"Ancient","text":"▸Dawn: Gain 1●.\n\n☾, Abandon a character: Gain 1●.","copies":2},
        {"id":"123baf70-305a-4583-bdba-a10b5153fbeb","name":"Dustborn Veteran","subtype":"Survivor","text":"When a non-figment survivor you control is dissolved, materialize a 1✦ survivor figment.","copies":2},
