    {
      "id": "tide-sig-05",
      "name": "Seraveth signature",
      "shortName": "Void Accelerant",
      "displayName": "Hunger of the Deep",
      "displayDescription": "Floods the void with the discarded and fallen, then unleashes a high-spark finisher.",
      "summary": "A survivor-heavy tide that deliberately floods the void through repeated erode triggers and cheap character play, then cashes in that void depth for a near-free high-spark finisher while dissolved-ally payoffs keep the hand full — distinguished from its nearest siblings by centering on void quantity as a resource rather than discard looping or abandon-for-energy ramp.",
      "description": "Tide-sig-05 is built around an unusually deep void-filling engine and the payoffs that exploit it. The backbone consists of characters that erode on materialization or dissolution — Searcher in the Mists erodes 4 both when it enters and when it is dissolved, Fargazer erodes 1 every time any character is played and then reclaims itself to repeat the effect, and Ashwalker erodes 3 on materialization. That steady void accumulation exists to enable the tide's marquee threat: Paradox Enforcer, which costs just 1● and hits for 7✦ once you banish 7 cards from your void, and can even be played from the void itself. Supporting the board in the meantime, Veil of the Wastes recurs from the void every time you materialize any character costing 2● or less, and Kindred Sparks plays for 1● whenever an allied survivor is in play, letting the tide sustain board presence cheaply while continuing to erode. When allies do fall, Soulreaver draws a card for each non-figment dissolution and Dustborn Veteran replaces dissolved survivors with figment tokens, converting challenge losses into a growing board. Compared to the Kael Voss tide — which shares the survivor and void-recursion shell but pivots into a discard-looping subgame with cards that draw, gain ●, or grow in power each time a card is discarded — Seraveth's tide treats the void as fuel to be burned rather than a trigger to be repeatedly activated; and unlike the Vaela tide, which uses abandonment to ramp energy through Nightmare Manifest and Exiles of the Last Light, this tide's abandon effects are secondary tools (Obliterator of Worlds, Kindlehorn) grafted onto a primary plan of out-eroding the opponent and slamming a seven-spark threat for one energy.",
      "color": "purple",
      "claims": {"tribe": "Survivor", "mechanics": ["abandon","discard","reclaim"]},
      "role": "signature",
      "dreamAvatarId": "6488452D-4E9E-466C-96DF-716D4EC646B1",
      "cards": [
        {"id":"123baf70-305a-4583-bdba-a10b5153fbeb","name":"Dustborn Veteran","subtype":"Survivor","text":"When a non-figment survivor you control is dissolved, materialize a 1✦ survivor figment.","copies":2},
        {"id":"1d92e103-8415-433d-97d6-ac8a83660b34","name":"Searcher in the Mists","subtype":"Survivor","text":"▸Materialized, Dissolved: Erode 4.","copies":2},
        {"id":"3a59cd3d-08a9-4a75-a5ab-c91b19d2d8c1","name":"Graywatch","subtype":"Survivor","text":"Vengeful\n\nWhen you play a card from your void, return this character to play.","copies":2},
