    {
      "id": "tide-sig-09",
      "name": "Edran signature",
      "shortName": "Evasive Outsider Draw",
      "displayName": "The Unseen Procession",
      "displayDescription": "Slips phasing Outsiders past every blocker, using removal and disruption to stop the opponent's plans.",
      "summary": "A tempo-control tide built on phasing outsiders that convert unblocked scores into card draw, snowballing evasive threats into overwhelming card advantage while light countermagic shields the engine — where its nearest sibling (tide-sig-10) shares the countermagic skeleton but pursues deck filtering, mass hand resets, and tutors instead of an evasion-driven draw engine.",
      "description": "Tide-sig-09 is an outsider-tempo tide built around phasing evaders that reward connecting unopposed. The draw core pairs Vanishing Inquisitor (\"when this character scores ⍟, draw a card, then discard a card\"), Thronebound Arbiter and Driftrider (\"when an allied outsider scores ⍟, draw a card\" — Driftrider also foreseeing 1), and Northlight Maestro (\"when this character scores ⍟, draw a card\"), so every evasive hit refills the hand and keeps the pressure compounding. A steady supply of evasive bodies comes from the outsider-figment package — Last Beacon (\"3●, ☾: materialize a 1✦ outsider figment\", and a draw-plus-⍟ payoff when an allied outsider scores) and Breach Artist — which dovetails with Edran's own ability to mint 1✦ outsider figments, letting the deck keep a phasing threat on board to carry its triggers. A light countermagic shell — Defiant Parry, Echoing Denial, Abolish, Crumbling Covenant — protects the engine through the assembly turns, while selection and refill from Sunset Chapel Rest, Crimson Pilgrimage, Fractured Veil, and Echoes of the Journey smooth draws and convert the card surplus into reach. Compared to tide-sig-10, which runs the same countermagic backbone but leans on deck filtering, mass hand resets, and tutors to sculpt a perfect hand, tide-sig-09 is defined by evasion and triggered draw: it wants an unblockable outsider on the board every turn and turns each connection into a card, grinding the opponent out under a rising tide of card advantage.",
      "color": "blue",
      "claims": {"tribe": "events", "mechanics": ["prevent","discard"]},
      "role": "signature",
      "dreamAvatarId": "5E28154D-770A-4B84-8AAC-9DE44F5D7D02",
