    {
      "id": "tide-sig-13",
      "name": "Ovanel signature",
      "shortName": "Event Storm Ramp",
      "displayName": "Gathering Tempest",
      "displayDescription": "Spins cheap events into surging power, then detonates them through copied, amplified effects.",
      "summary": "This tide generates energy through repeated cheap events and converts that surplus into copied or scaled spells, differentiating itself from its nearest sibling by centering on event-copy payoffs and energy acceleration rather than a character-board discard engine.",
      "description": "Tide-sig-13 is an event-heavy deck (roughly 60% events) built around two interlocking loops: energy generation and event multiplication. Cheap ramp events like Arc Gate Opening (gain 4●), Data Pulse (gain 2● and draw), and Genesis Burst (double current ●) fund the tide's mid-game, while Starcatcher — which gains 1● each time you play an event — sustains momentum turn over turn. The event-copy suite (Twice-Lit Portal copies the next event you play, Cascading Detonation copies it twice while reclaiming 5●, Cascade of Reflections copies every event until end of turn) converts that energy surplus into outsized turns where a single removal or draw spell does two or three times its face-value work. Discard-based draw keeps the hand full: Sunken Radiance draws two and discards two while reclaiming energy, Iconoclast trades a discard for two ephemeral draws, and Wandering Archivist accrues ⍟ on every discard as a secondary scoring line. The void naturally grows through this cycling, enabling Weight of Memory — a free fast interrupt that dissolves any enemy whose ✦ is at most the number of cards in your void — to handle threats that would otherwise require dedicated removal. Where the closest sibling tide leans on characters that gain ✦ from discard stacks (Minstrel of Falling Light growing with each event in void, Call of the Lost flooding the board with awakened ember figments), this tide treats characters primarily as event-enablers and energy engines, with the payoff living in the events themselves rather than in an accumulating board.",
      "color": "blue",
      "claims": {"tribe": "events", "mechanics": ["discard","reclaim","ramp"]},
      "role": "signature",
      "dreamAvatarId": "F6208407-C4E9-42AC-B533-346704F5E39E",
