    {
      "id": "tide-sig-15",
      "name": "Grath signature",
      "shortName": "Spirit Animal Flood",
      "displayName": "Stampede Unbound",
      "displayDescription": "Floods the field with cheap Spirit Animals and converts the horde into one crushing finish.",
      "summary": "A spirit animal flooding engine that ramps energy through Dawn triggers on cheap creatures and converts a wide board into an overwhelming finish, distinguished from its nearest sibling by leaning into board-wide character-play synergies — Conduit of Resonance chains Dawn triggers across all allies on every character played, and Cindermarch mass-awakens the board on materialization — rather than single-champion burst or hand-filtering loops.",
      "description": "Tide-sig-15 is overwhelmingly a spirit animal deck: over 85% of its copies are characters, dominated by cheap 1● spirit animals that each read \"▸Dawn: Gain 1●,\" collectively forming a self-sustaining energy engine. Cards like Skyborne Jellyfish (gain 1● per allied ≤2● cost character on Dawn), Undying Fang (Dawn ramp scaling with spirit animal count), and Melodist of the Finale (gain 1● each time you play a character) let the deck snowball its energy pool simply by deploying its creatures. That energy feeds mass-pump finishers: Spiritbound Alpha (5● to give all spirit animals +3✦ and vengeful until end of turn), Mystic Runefish (sets every spirit animal's ✦ to 7), and Spirit Bond (all characters gain +X✦ equal to ally count). What distinguishes this tide from its nearest sibling is a set of board-wide character-play amplifiers unique to this pool: Conduit of Resonance re-fires the ▸Dawn ability of every other allied character each time you play one, turning a single character play into a burst of energy triggers across the whole board, and Cindermarch awakens every other ally whenever you materialize a character, enabling the awakened-cost abilities that power the support engine. Alongside Petal-Seer at two copies — which lets you play characters directly off the top of your deck when you have three or more allies — the tide sustains its flood through the midgame and closes decisively through the mass-pump payoffs.",
      "color": "green",
      "claims": {"tribe": "Spirit Animal", "mechanics": ["ramp"]},
      "role": "signature",
      "dreamAvatarId": "94E7C651-25E9-4A62-9DE4-EAF5BA20542C",
      "cards": [
        {"id":"07ceb104-0b27-473a-bc72-e6225479ed83","name":"Stoneborn Leviathan","subtype":"Spirit Animal","text":"1●, Return a character you control to hand: Give a character you control +1✦.","copies":2},
