    {
      "id": "tide-sig-19",
      "name": "Tensho signature",
      "shortName": "Warrior Void Recursion",
      "displayName": "The Returning Legion",
      "displayDescription": "Cycles Warriors back from the void, turning every fall into renewed, relentless pressure.",
      "summary": "A warrior tribal deck built around dissolve-triggered void recursion and draw, generating sustained pressure by cycling warriors back from the void and converting their deaths into card advantage — contrasting with the nearest sibling that focuses on producing 1✦ figment tokens, and the other sibling that emphasizes climbing ✦ values through abandon-and-pump chains.",
      "description": "Tide-sig-19 is an overwhelmingly character-heavy warrior deck (101 of 110 copies are characters) whose central engine runs on dissolve triggers and void returns. The core loop is powered by multiple 2x warriors that retrieve fallen allies: one returns a warrior with lesser cost from the void whenever any allied warrior is dissolved, another returns a different warrior from the void when it itself dissolves, and a third does the same on its own dissolution. Alongside these, a draw-on-materialize-and-dissolve warrior ensures that the constant flow of warriors in and out of the void converts into cards, while a 4-cost character pumps itself each turn and draws a card for each spark it has accumulated when it finally dissolves. Support payoffs scale directly off the warrior count — a commander that gives every warrior +1✦ at dawn, a fast event that grants an ally +1✦ per allied warrior, and a 5-cost finisher that costs 1● less for each ally in play — so the recursion engine both refuels the board and makes those payoffs hit harder. The tide also carries a void-cheat package unique among its siblings: a 4-cost explorer that materializes a ≤2● cost character from the void whenever a warrior is played, and a tinkerer that abandons a warrior to discover and directly materialize a warrior with 1● higher cost. Compared to its nearest sibling, which centers on churning out 1✦ warrior figments through dedicated token producers and converts those tokens with a figment-payoff engine, tide-sig-19 invests that slot space in resilient, self-replacing warriors that grind value through individual dissolve triggers rather than raw board width; and compared to the second-nearest sibling, which stacks +✦ through abandon-and-pump repeaters and a high-cost ⧗-removal outlet, tide-sig-19 prioritizes card flow and recursive board presence over concentrating spark on individual threats.",
      "color": "yellow",
      "claims": {"tribe": "Warrior", "mechanics": ["abandon","figment"]},
      "role": "signature",
      "dreamAvatarId": "BF72ADFF-7D74-4BE8-9B93-1DB7BA13A1DB",
