    {
      "id": "tide-fac-02",
      "name": "Lean: Clockwork Conductor",
      "shortName": "Abandon Score Engine",
      "displayName": "Offerings of Worth",
      "displayDescription": "Converts sacrificed allies into points, power, and cards, recycling its best pieces.",
      "summary": "A character-dense sacrifice deck that converts abandoning allies into score (⍟), energy (●), and cards, then recycles key pieces through a reclaim loop — where the nearest sibling tide-fac-14 pursues a survivor-tribal token strategy around dissolve triggers instead.",
      "description": "Tide-fac-02 is built almost entirely of characters (41 of 45 cards) and operates on a two-part engine: repeatedly abandoning allies to generate score and resources, then reclaiming certain characters from the void to do it again. The abandon-as-action core is reinforced at double copies: Stargazer Adrift turns an abandonment into Foresee 1, Harvester of Despair converts one into a permanent +1✦, and Exiles of the Last Light pays out a full energy with each sacrifice. On top of those activations, passive dissolve-watchers — Silent Avenger, Skull Weaver, and Avatar of Cosmic Reckoning each gaining 1⍟ whenever characters leave play — mean that the act of feeding the engine also accumulates score directly. The mid-range payoffs escalate this further: Soulreaver and Deathwalker draw a card each time a non-figment or survivor ally is dissolved, Scuttled Fortune (fast) converts a multi-dissolve turn into a full refill, and Volcanic Channeler banks an energy for every ally lost. The reclaim package — Rusted Monolith, Enginespeaker, Torn Circuit Feeder, and Titan of Forgotten Echoes — keeps the engine fueled by ensuring sacrificed pieces return rather than stay banished. Compared to the nearest sibling tide-fac-14, which concentrates on survivor tribal density (Kindred Sparks, Shadowcaller, Sorrow Watcher, Tidewreck Navigator) and dissolve-triggered token generation, tide-fac-02 is less concerned with subtype counts and more focused on the abandon action itself as the primary resource-generating event, backed by a reclaim loop that tide-fac-14 does not develop.",
      "color": "orange",
      "claims": {"tribe": "Survivor", "mechanics": ["abandon","reclaim","figment"]},
      "role": "facet",
      "leanCardId": "9adbe3db-d872-4b75-92b5-d7f2798c22ce",
