    {
      "id": "tide-fac-03",
      "name": "Lean: Flash of Power",
      "shortName": "Event Storm Combo",
      "displayName": "The Worldbreaker",
      "displayDescription": "Builds toward one explosive turn, detonating stored power into copied, chained events.",
      "summary": "This tide builds toward a single explosive turn by ramping energy through cheap bursts and event-triggered refunds, then detonating that energy into copied and chained events — distinguishing itself from the nearest sibling (tide-fac-20) by centering on mass-copy finishers and void-depth payoffs rather than steady draw-filter and token production.",
      "description": "Tide-fac-03 is an event-heavy (34 events, 11 characters) tide built around assembling and then firing a single high-power turn. The energy ramp layer comes from cheap events like Arc Gate Opening (1-cost, gain 4●), Canopy of Stars, Genesis Burst (double current ●), and the character Starcatcher (gain 1● per event played), which together allow a mid-to-late turn to generate far more energy than normal. That energy is then multiplied through event-copy effects: Echo Architect (2x) copies every event you play at a 1● premium, Cascade of Reflections (2x) copies each event until end of turn, and Cascading Detonation (2x) copies the next event played twice and can be reclaimed for 5● to set up another chain — these three together form the core combo-engine. The payoff events cash in the volume of spells played: Hatching Ground erodes X equal to cards played this turn, and Echoes of the Journey draws a free ephemeral card for each card already played, extending the chain mid-storm. A void-reclaim sub-package (From the Barrow granting mass-reclaim to all void events, Archive of the Forgotten, Weblight Waif returning events from the void) and void-scaling threats like Minstrel of Falling Light and Weight of Memory give the tide a secondary dimension of depth-over-time. Compared to its nearest sibling tide-fac-20, which shares the event-copy infrastructure but distinguishes itself with Broadcast Array's ⍟ payoff, sustained draw filtering through Spiral Offering and Desperation, and a stronger token-production angle via Call of the Lost at 2x, tide-fac-03 instead doubles down on Cascading Detonation as its signature finisher and features Genesis Burst plus Reunion as turn-reset/storm enablers — making it a bigger-swing, fewer-boards, combo-oriented version of the same event-heavy archetype.",
      "color": "blue",
      "claims": {"tribe": "events", "mechanics": ["discard","ramp","copy"]},
      "role": "facet",
      "leanCardId": "c430ed7b-523e-4580-9a53-d43d11265633",
      "cards": [
        {"id":"21965e95-0c8c-470c-a1e1-06d7b87a8d00","name":"Echo Architect","subtype":"Tinkerer","text":"Events cost you 1● more.\n\nWhen you play an event, copy it.","copies":2},
        {"id":"29d25251-8b42-4d3d-97e6-6c3abaabd9a2","name":"Blooming Horror","text":"Choose a player. For each card you've played this turn, that player erodes 2.","copies":2},
        {"id":"4752fc43-6696-4bc3-88d0-4d5b97622fa8","name":"From the Barrow","text":"Until end of turn, events in your void gain reclaim.\n\nWhen you discard or erode this card, it gains reclaim 3●.","copies":2},
        {"id":"91d9afed-ea29-43af-9021-0f3ecbdc252e","name":"Starcatcher","subtype":"Visitor","text":"When you play an event, gain 1●.","copies":2},
        {"id":"995c570b-2d86-4f6f-8f02-dd0902e32fcd","name":"Ritekeeper","subtype":"Explorer","text":"Discard a card: Choose an event in your void to gain reclaim.","copies":2},
        {"id":"b957466e-f748-4a95-89b2-8509dc762223","name":"Trance Diviner","subtype":"Visionary","text":"Discard a card: Draw two cards with ephemeral.","copies":2},
        {"id":"be72bd04-21a6-4035-a117-2b7213ad1a34","name":"Arc Gate Opening","text":"Gain 4●.","copies":2},
        {"id":"fb967cc1-4199-4a08-8070-724e07cebea5","name":"Entropy Cascade","text":"The next time you play an event this turn, copy it twice.\n\nReclaim 5●.","copies":2},
        {"id":"fc4b06d6-3b30-4769-af98-88fcea5b54dd","name":"Cascade of Reflections","text":"Until end of turn, when you play an event, copy it.","copies":2},
