    {
      "id": "tide-fac-06",
      "name": "Lean: Paradox Corps Enforcer",
      "shortName": "Bounce & Disruption",
      "displayName": "The Shifting Tide",
      "displayDescription": "Outmaneuvers foes with disruption, sculpting, and a relentless return-to-hand control engine.",
      "summary": "A control tide that combines hand disruption, topdeck sculpting, and a bounce-value engine to outmaneuver opponents, distinguishing itself from its nearest siblings by leaning into return-to-hand loops and board-clearing event accumulation rather than hard counterspells and void-reclaim.",
      "description": "This tide runs an even split of characters and events, with its mechanical identity anchored by two interlocking threads: bounce value and hand disruption. The bounce engine centers on cards that return characters to hand — Ridgecutter (return a character, gain 2●), Annular Recall (return a character of cost X, draw a card), and Headtaker Wurm (a phasing body that returns an enemy on materialization) — all supercharged by Breach Artist, which reduces a returned ally's cost by 2● each time it comes back to hand. A second thread runs through hand disruption: multiple effects let you discard or banish specific cards from the opponent's hand, giving the tide strong pre-emptive answers to threats before they ever resolve. Topdeck sculpting ties the two threads together, with Planetgazer (foresee 2 on materialize, appearing at two copies) and several low-cost foresee and filtering events ensuring the right bounce targets or disruption pieces arrive on schedule. The Waking Titan serves as a late finisher by storing one counter each time you play an event, then spending five to return all other characters to hand — a board wipe earned by maintaining the dense event-play the rest of the tide naturally encourages. Where the nearest siblings (tide-fac-07 and tide-fac-23) invest heavily in a hard counterspell suite — running double copies of Defiant Parry and Abolish plus Ripple Through Reality — and lean on void-reclaim loops for card advantage, this tide instead converts bounce and hand stripping into incremental resource gains, with fewer clean \"prevent a played card\" answers but far more proactive ways to keep the opponent from ever building a threatening board.",
      "color": "blue",
      "claims": {"tribe": "events", "mechanics": ["prevent"]},
      "role": "facet",
      "leanCardId": "954e8d50-d494-4fb2-b4c7-74979083b774",
