    {
      "id": "tide-fac-12",
      "name": "Lean: Cloudmantle Ray",
      "shortName": "Spirit Animal Swarm",
      "displayName": "One Pack, One Strike",
      "displayDescription": "Races to unify a board of cheap Spirit Animals into towering threats.",
      "summary": "A warrior-dense tide that uses dissolution triggers to continuously refuel hand and board from the void, distinguished from its closest sibling by centering on automatic dissolved-triggered recursion rather than deliberate abandonment for energy.",
      "description": "Tide-fac-12 is built almost entirely of warriors (42 of 45 copies) and organizes itself around a tight chain of dissolution triggers that keep the hand and board stocked. The anchor engine is Burning Revenant (2 copies): whenever any allied warrior is dissolved, it automatically returns a warrior with lesser cost from the void to hand, creating a self-replenishing loop every time a warrior dies. Multiple other pieces reinforce this directly — Infernal Cavalier and Starbound Striker each trigger on their own dissolution to return another warrior from the void, and Cinderblade Legionnaire does the same while also carrying Vengeful. A mass-resurrection payoff arrives in Wake the Fallen, which materializes all characters that dissolved in the same turn, converting a bad challenge into a sudden board refill. Inferno's Herald adds a second dimension: it accumulates +✦ each dawn and, when dissolved, spawns a wave of 1✦ warrior figments equal to its spark total, rewarding the player for letting it grow before trading it away. Where the closely related sibling tide (Lean: Burning Revenant) pairs its dissolution-return warriors with Blood Reaver as a 2x card — deliberately abandoning warriors to generate energy — this tide treats abandonment as incidental and instead stacks dissolved-trigger recursion pieces so that blocking challengers and losing warriors becomes a source of card advantage and tempo rather than a cost to pay.",
      "color": "yellow",
      "claims": {"tribe": "Spirit Animal", "mechanics": ["ramp"]},
      "role": "facet",
      "leanCardId": "0f1ac858-a28a-489b-9dd4-4d28f8f1abf5",
      "cards": [
        {"id":"3cda9dd7-cb81-43c1-9db5-1444d7363e13","name":"Spirit Bond","text":"Until end of turn, characters you control have +X✦ where X is the number of characters you control.","copies":2},
        {"id":"4e3c04a9-1cdd-468a-b42a-40157ed9c9d6","name":"Eternal Stag","subtype":"Spirit Animal","text":"Support – Supported spirit animals have +1✦.\n\n2●, ☾: Draw a spirit animal.","copies":2},
        {"id":"965ce3b2-a722-475c-99c5-5b35685d2404","name":"Dreamvale Monarch","subtype":"Spirit Animal","text":"▸Materialized: Draw a card.","copies":2},
        {"id":"c8579b20-95ff-4b1d-b4c6-6bd049fc4760","name":"Ghostlight Wolves","subtype":"Spirit Animal","text":"Support – Supported spirit animals have +2✦.\n\n☾: Gain 1● for each spirit animal you control.","copies":2},
        {"id":"caaee8a9-0c22-41b4-950f-4c1131b98221","name":"Celestial Reverie","text":"Until end of turn, when you play a character, draw a card.","copies":2},
