    {
      "id": "tide-fac-14",
      "name": "Lean: Chaos Crasher",
      "shortName": "Warrior Blood Ramp",
      "displayName": "Bloodforged Vanguard",
      "displayDescription": "Sacrifices Warriors for energy, then rebuilds through figments, recursion, and scaling commanders.",
      "summary": "A warrior-heavy sacrifice ramp tide that converts warriors into energy and replacement bodies, then uses wide-board support and void-return effects to keep pressure after challenge trades.",
      "description": "This tide is almost entirely characters (43 of 45 copies), with warriors making up the clear center of gravity. Its strongest repeat is Blood Reaver at two copies, turning abandoned warriors into 2● bursts that fund larger plays and activated abilities. The deck has several ways to make those sacrifices productive instead of merely costly: Spellweaver replaces non-figment warriors with 1✦ warrior figments, Standard Bearer and Voidsire create more warrior bodies as characters or warriors are played, Crescendo Channeler produces a warrior figment at Dawn and can cash a wide board into energy, and Mirror Protocol upgrades an abandoned warrior into a higher-cost warrior. The rest of the shell lets the warband survive attrition: Burning Revenant, Cinderblade Legionnaire, Starbound Striker, and Infernal Cavalier return warriors from the void, while Dream Garden Visitor and Chaos Crasher provide additional void access. Skyflame Commander and Battlefield Medic are the doubled support pieces that turn the board into real challenge pressure, with Wolfbond Chieftain and Dreadmount Sovereign adding further warrior-count payoffs. The identity is sacrifice-powered warrior ramp with token and recursion support.",
      "color": "yellow",
      "claims": {"tribe": "Warrior", "mechanics": ["abandon"]},
      "role": "facet",
      "leanCardId": "ed4d5342-0690-40b7-ab48-6b76035466f2",
      "cards": [
