    {
      "id": "tide-fac-19",
      "name": "Lean: Call the Lost",
      "shortName": "Event Count Combo",
      "displayName": "The Quickening Chain",
      "displayDescription": "Spins a high-velocity run of events, cashing in the played card count for victory.",
      "summary": "This tide builds a high-velocity event chain — ramping energy through Arc Gate Opening, Flash of Power, and Starcatcher, then cashing in cards-played-this-turn counters for erosion (Hatching Ground), score (Broadcast Array), and a refueling draw (Echoes of the Journey) — distinguishing itself from its closest sibling, Flash of Power, which centers on detonation-copy bombs rather than accumulating turn-count payoffs.",
      "description": "Tide-fac-20 is an event-heavy combo tide (34 events, 11 characters) built around playing as many events as possible in a single turn and converting that count into compounding payoffs. The energy ramp suite — Arc Gate Opening (\"Gain 4●\"), Flash of Power (\"Gain 5●\"), Starcatcher (\"When you play an event, gain 1●\"), and Data Pulse (\"Gain 2●. Draw a card\") — lets the player chain events in rapid succession, while Echo Architect (\"When you play an event, copy it\") and Cascade of Reflections multiply that output. The cards-played count then fuels Hatching Ground (\"For each card you've played this turn, chosen player erodes X\") for proportional board erosion, Broadcast Array (\"Gain 2⍟ for each card you have played this turn\") for direct scoring, and Echoes of the Journey (\"For each card you have played this turn, draw a card with ephemeral; they cost 0●\") to extend the chain further. A supporting void-reclaim package — From the Barrow, Archive of the Forgotten, and Dreadwood Emissary — lets key events loop back for repeated use. Compared to its nearest sibling, Flash of Power, which instead double-weights Cascading Detonation (\"copy it twice, Reclaim 5●\") and Genesis Burst (\"Double your current ●\") to build toward a single explosive copy detonation, this tide favors stringing many moderate events together and cashing the running count as score and erosion; and unlike the Scorched Reckoning sibling, it carries no ⧗-counter characters and minimal removal, fully committing to the velocity-and-payoff gameplan over board control.",
      "color": "blue",
      "claims": {"tribe": "events", "mechanics": ["discard","reclaim","ramp"]},
      "role": "facet",
      "leanCardId": "2690912e-0295-4d12-a603-5946d37902d3",
      "cards": [
        {"id":"29d25251-8b42-4d3d-97e6-6c3abaabd9a2","name":"Blooming Horror","text":"Choose a player. For each card you've played this turn, that player erodes 2.","copies":2},
        {"id":"4752fc43-6696-4bc3-88d0-4d5b97622fa8","name":"From the Barrow","text":"Until end of turn, events in your void gain reclaim.\n\nWhen you discard or erode this card, it gains reclaim 3●.","copies":2},
        {"id":"91d9afed-ea29-43af-9021-0f3ecbdc252e","name":"Starcatcher","subtype":"Visitor","text":"When you play an event, gain 1●.","copies":2},
        {"id":"995c570b-2d86-4f6f-8f02-dd0902e32fcd","name":"Ritekeeper","subtype":"Explorer","text":"Discard a card: Choose an event in your void to gain reclaim.","copies":2},
        {"id":"b957466e-f748-4a95-89b2-8509dc762223","name":"Trance Diviner","subtype":"Visionary","text":"Discard a card: Draw two cards with ephemeral.","copies":2},
        {"id":"be72bd04-21a6-4035-a117-2b7213ad1a34","name":"Arc Gate Opening","text":"Gain 4●.","copies":2},
