    {
      "id": "tide-fac-20",
      "name": "Lean: Vigilant Howler",
      "shortName": "Spirit Animal ✦ Scaling",
      "displayName": "Feral Surge",
      "displayDescription": "Scales a pack of Spirit Animals through blessings and a unifying surge to a crushing finish.",
      "summary": "A spirit animal flood deck that scales ✦ through Support effects and Mystic Runefish's mass equalization, then closes with Spirit Bond — distinct from its siblings by doubling its draw-on-play burst (two Celestial Reveries) while skipping the discover-chain engine and Sunshadow Eagle accumulation that define those other builds.",
      "description": "Tide-fac-21 is a character-heavy spirit animal swarm built around stacking ✦ on a wide board and cashing it in with a single decisive push. The dominant engine runs through two copies each of Celestial Reverie (\"when you play a character, draw a card\"), Ghostlight Wolves (Support: supported spirit animals have +2✦; tap for 1● per allied spirit animal), and Mystic Runefish (5●, tap: each allied spirit animal's ✦ becomes 7), with Eternal Stag providing additional Support (+1✦ to supported spirit animals) and tutoring for more spirit animals. The play pattern is to flood the board with cheap spirit animals — many with Dawn ramp triggers that convert board width into energy — then use Ghostlight Wolves and Eternal Stag to boost supported allies, and fire Mystic Runefish to equalize every spirit animal's ✦ to 7 before landing Spirit Bond for a massive lethal swing. Unlike tide-fac-05, which centers Sunshadow Eagle at two copies and converts ⧗ accumulation into late energy bursts, this tide drops the Eagle to a single copy and instead runs double Celestial Reverie to keep the hand fueled while deploying the wide board. Unlike tide-fac-13, which doubles both Dreamcatcher's Call and Shatterpoint Agent to build a discover-chain toolbox that finds specific finishers at any cost, this tide invests that slot count directly into ✦ amplification through Support, making its gameplan more linear but more explosive when Mystic Runefish resolves on a full board.",
      "color": "green",
      "claims": {"tribe": "Spirit Animal", "mechanics": ["ramp"]},
      "role": "facet",
      "leanCardId": "61060827-8bed-4b63-b63d-6c3b0536e941",
