    {
      "id": "tide-fac-21",
      "name": "Lean: Lumin-Gate Seer",
      "shortName": "Spirit Animal Spark Pump",
      "displayName": "The Roaring Throng",
      "displayDescription": "Floods with cheap Spirit Animals, then stacks blessings into a board-wide, high-spark charge.",
      "summary": "This tide floods the board with cheap Spirit Animals, then amplifies their spark through stacking Support bonuses and Mystic Runefish's equalizing ability, closing with Spirit Bond's board-wide high-spark finisher — where the closest sibling (fac-05) emphasizes Dawn energy generation and ⧗ accumulation instead, and fac-04 leans on cost reduction and discover chains rather than spark scaling.",
      "description": "Tide-fac-22 is a character-dense spirit animal swarm built around layered spark amplification. The core engine runs through Ghostlight Wolves (Support: supported spirit animals have +2✦), Eternal Stag (Support: supported spirit animals have +1✦, plus a 2●/tap tutor to draw more spirit animals), and Mystic Runefish (5●/tap: every allied spirit animal's ✦ becomes 7) — three 2x cards that together convert a wide, cheap board into a formation of high-✦ threats. Dreamvale Monarch and Celestial Reverie (both at 2x) keep the hand full while playing out characters, sustaining the flood of bodies needed to trigger Support bonuses and maximize Spirit Bond's payoff. The finisher is Spirit Bond (2x, 7 cost): until end of turn, all allied characters have +X✦ where X equals the number of allied characters, rewarding the widest possible board. A secondary discover-and-upgrade layer — Lumin-Gate Seer drawing on cost-matched materializations, Curio Dealer trading a character for a higher-value one, Shatterpoint Agent discarding to discover a character of greater cost — provides mid-game card selection without committing to a purely linear plan. Compared to the nearest sibling fac-05, which shares many spirit animal pieces but doubles on Skyborne Jellyfish's Dawn energy generation and Sunshadow Eagle's ⧗ accumulation for energy bursts, this tide is less focused on energy production and more focused on ✦ totals: it runs two copies of Mystic Runefish (absent at 2x in fac-05) and treats the Support payoff as its primary scaling mechanism rather than a side benefit of a Dawn-ramp strategy.",
      "color": "green",
      "claims": {"tribe": "Spirit Animal", "mechanics": ["ramp"]},
