    {
      "id": "tide-fac-22",
      "name": "Lean: Impending Fury",
      "shortName": "Outsider Score Engine",
      "displayName": "Wardens of the Threshold",
      "displayDescription": "Prevents the opponent's cards, while scoring Outsiders chain into draw and mounting points.",
      "summary": "A countermagic-heavy outsider tribal tide that chains draw and ⍟ generation off scoring outsiders, distinguished from its Driftrider sibling by deeper outsider-payoff redundancy and richer interrupt counterspell density rather than bounce/return-to-hand tricks or opponent hand disruption.",
      "description": "This tide splits evenly between characters and events, with its central engine built around outsider characters that reward scoring ⍟: Last Beacon generates a 1✦ outsider figment and draws a card while gaining ⍟ equal to the scoring outsider's cost, Thronebound Arbiter (the tide's highest-copy character) draws a card whenever any allied outsider scores, and Driftrider foresees and draws on the same trigger. That scoring loop is protected by a dense interrupt suite — double Defiant Parry (offering counterspell unless the opponent pays 1●), Abolish, Echoing Denial, Keeper of the Tides, Null Sphere, Momentum of the Fallen, and Ripple Through Reality together — which keeps the opponent from disrupting the outsider board while ⍟ accumulates toward Standoff's instant-speed dissolve. The draw events (double Fragments of Vision, Crimson Pilgrimage, Sunset Chapel Rest, Miraculous Arrival) refuel the hand and ensure counterspells remain available at all times. Compared to the Driftrider sibling tide, which trades some counterspell depth for a bounce-and-redeploy subtheme (Breach Artist, Annular Recall, Cosmic Puppeteer) and heavier hand-disruption tools (The Thinning, Lurking Dread, Clockwork Prodigy's blanket offering), this tide runs double Thronebound Arbiter and the full set of interrupt events to maximize the reliability and redundancy of the outsider-score draw engine.",
      "color": "blue",
      "claims": {"tribe": "events", "mechanics": ["prevent"]},
