    {
      "id": "tide-fac-29",
      "name": "Lean: Harbor Warden",
      "shortName": "Warrior Recursion Draw",
      "displayName": "Harbor's Returning Blades",
      "displayDescription": "Draws through Warrior pressure, sacrificing and recurring the warband to keep challenges flowing.",
      "summary": "A warrior-dense draw and recursion tide that uses Harbor Warden, Bloomweaver, Blood Reaver, and multiple void-return warriors to turn a steady warband into cards, energy, and repeat pressure.",
      "description": "This is a 43-character warrior tide with only two events, so its card flow and resilience come from the board itself. Harbor Warden is the lean anchor, providing a materialized draw-two body inside a shell that already wants to play and replay warriors. Bloomweaver draws on both materialization and dissolution, Silent Observer draws when the opponent plays events, Blood Moon Ronin can abandon itself for an ephemeral card, Blood Altar Monarch turns two abandoned warriors into another card, and Tranquil Duelist draws on dissolution based on its ✦. The energy and sacrifice axis is still important: two Blood Reavers convert abandoned warriors into 2●, two Ethereal Trailblazers reward maintaining three warriors, and Crescendo Channeler or Wolfbond Chieftain can transform a broad warrior board into more energy. The recursion layer is dense enough to make trades attractive, with Burning Revenant, Cinderblade Legionnaire, Starbound Striker, Infernal Cavalier, Prism Caller, Dream Garden Visitor, and The Deathsworn all returning or replaying warriors from the void. Compared to the nearby Chaos Crasher facet, this tide leans less on support pieces and more on drawing cards while warriors die, return, and get sacrificed for energy.",
      "color": "orange",
      "claims": {"tribe": "Warrior", "mechanics": ["abandon"]},
