    {
      "id": "tide-neu-03",
      "name": "Broad: Gloomantler / Dustborn Veteran",
      "shortName": "Energy Ramp Abandon",
      "displayName": "Rising Power",
      "displayDescription": "Burns sacrifices into vast stores of power for discoveries and towering threats.",
      "summary": "A broad abandon-fueled energy ramp deck that converts character sacrifices and low-cost triggers into large ● stores for discover payoffs and big materialization, distinguishing itself from sibling abandon tides by prioritizing energy acceleration over dissolve removal or doubled-up abandon-for-draw engines.",
      "description": "Tide-neu-03 is a character-heavy (24 of 30 cards) deck built around two interlocking axes: abandoning cheap characters to generate value and accruing large amounts of energy (●) to fuel expensive payoffs. The energy ramp package is unusually dense — free or near-free gain-3● events, a Spirit Animal that gains 2● every Dawn cycle, another that gains 2● on materialization, Entropy Spike gaining 1● or +1 maximum ● when dissolved, and Volcanic Channeler converting every dissolved ally into a ● — meaning the deck can reach far above its natural ● ceiling. That accumulated energy feeds discover tools like Rite of Summoning (discover a card of cost X) and Door to Possibility (discover an event of cost X), and powers Stolen Genesis, which abandons a character to immediately materialize a random higher-cost character from the deck. The closest sibling, tide-neu-09, shares many of the same survivors and abandon triggers but leans heavily into on-demand dissolve removal (fast interrupt events that dissolve enemies) and draw-on-dissolve payoffs such as Scuttled Fortune and Deathwalker; its end-game is board control through elimination rather than energy surplus. The other close sibling, the Shadowbinder facet tide, doubles up its core abandon cards (two copies each of Harvester of Despair, Skull Weaver, Kindred Sparks, Exiles of the Last Light, and Stolen Genesis) for a tight, self-consistent abandon engine focused on ⍟ accumulation and recurring void characters — a narrower and more redundant package than neu-03's wider spread of energy generation, discover selection, and survivor-figment production.",
      "color": "orange",
      "claims": {"mechanics": ["abandon","ramp"]},
      "role": "neutral",
      "leanCardId": "20fd609a-7529-4582-a362-b8151b0ae011",
      "cards": [
        {"id":"041fafeb-f159-4aba-90c2-3ce4b3038bdc","name":"Gloomantler","subtype":"Ancient","text":"Once per turn, if you have one or fewer cards in hand, you may play a character from your void.","copies":1},
        {"id":"123baf70-305a-4583-bdba-a10b5153fbeb","name":"Dustborn Veteran","subtype":"Survivor","text":"When a non-figment survivor you control is dissolved, materialize a 1✦ survivor figment.","copies":1},
        {"id":"1658d9a0-c3b0-4eb7-babc-4933acf362c4","name":"Glimpse of Infinity","text":"Gain 3●.","copies":1},
