    {
      "id": "tide-neu-08",
      "name": "Broad: Soulkindler / Angel of Memory",
      "shortName": "Void Cycling Recursion",
      "displayName": "The Eternal Cycle",
      "displayDescription": "Cycles cheap bodies through the void for bonuses and draw, reclaiming them again and again.",
      "summary": "A cheap-character recursion engine that deliberately cycles ≤2● characters through the void to unlock void-count bonuses and draw, then recurs them repeatedly — distinct from sibling spirit animal energy decks that flood the board for Dawn triggers, and from sacrifice-for-removal archetypes that treat abandoning as a cost to destroy enemies.",
      "description": "Tide-neu-08 is a character-dense deck (27 of 30 cards are characters) built almost entirely on cheap ≤2● bodies that rotate through the void as both fuel and payoff. The central loop involves deliberately abandoning or spending cheap characters to fill the void, then drawing value from Ferryman of the Falls (\"when a ≤2● cost character is put into your void, draw a card\") and powering up Abomination of Memory (which gains +4✦ whenever three or more ≤2● characters sit in the void). Scrap Reclaimer, Starsea Traveler, and Clockwork Conductor all return ≤2● characters from the void back to hand or play, sustaining the cycle turn after turn, while Veilseeker can return the entire cohort at once for a burst refill. Payoffs scale with the engine: Carrion Lord materializes a 4✦ monstrosity figment each time a ≤2● character is abandoned, Virtuoso of Harmony converts each such abandon into 1●, and The Forsaker converts each into 1⍟, rewarding repeated sacrifice with both mana acceleration and challenge threat generation. The nearest siblings, tide-sig-15 and tide-sig-16, also interact with ≤2● characters but their identity is spirit animal tribal momentum — Dawn-trigger energy from Skyborne Jellyfish and Undying Fang, pack-wide buffs from Ghostlight Wolves and Spiritbound Alpha, and flooding the board rather than cycling through it. Tide-sig-05 uses abandoning as a cost too, but to fuel dissolve removal (Maelstrom Denial, Together Against the Tide) and ⍟ engines, not to stack the void for recursion bonuses. Tide-neu-08's distinctive play pattern is a mid-game grind loop where cheap bodies continually re-enter the void and return to hand, generating incremental card draw, mana, and a steadily growing threat in Abomination of Memory and Carrion Lord's figments.",
      "color": "purple",
      "claims": {"mechanics": ["abandon"]},
      "role": "neutral",
      "leanCardId": "fa036c27-2234-4f76-8857-c242530627ce",
      "cards": [
        {"id":"4edf2d8d-61e4-4c3a-a388-4b52b2ebd005","name":"Soulkindler","subtype":"Survivor","text":"Abandon this character: Return a character from your void to your hand.\n\n▸Dawn: If this card is in your void, erode 3.","copies":2},
        {"id":"86881031-393f-4359-96f5-3adde6bdd74d","name":"Angel of Memory","subtype":"Visitor","text":"This character has +4✦ if there are three or more ≤2● cost characters in your void.","copies":2},
        {"id":"975f49d3-213a-43fc-8079-5fe40f126a7b","name":"Void Salvager","subtype":"Entity","text":"Awakened\n\n2●, ☾, Discard a card: Return up to two ≤2● cost characters from your void to your hand.","copies":2},
        {"id":"bd43b120-2503-406c-8b72-ea3dc55198a0","name":"Reckless Vigilante","subtype":"Super","text":"❖❖ – Abandon another character: A character you control cannot be targeted by effects this turn.","copies":2},
        {"id":"017a7b4b-3ccf-4635-9956-28a72b22274e","name":"Remnant Scavenger","subtype":"Monster","text":"This character has +1✦ for each ≤2● cost character in your void.\n\n☾, Discard a card: Draw a ≤2● cost character.","copies":1},
