    {
      "id": "tide-neu-11",
      "name": "Broad: Kindred Sparks / Silent Mourner",
      "shortName": "Abandon Energy Harvest",
      "displayName": "The Cull's Bounty",
      "displayDescription": "Converts abandons allies into power and points behind an efficient, resilient chain.",
      "summary": "A character-dense abandon-and-dissolve engine that converts sacrificed allies into energy (●) and dream (⍟) while Avatar of Cosmic Reckoning and Kindred Sparks anchor an efficient survivor chain — distinguishing it from the nearest sibling (tide-fac-24) by prioritizing energy ramp and ⍟ harvesting over survivor-subtype recursion loops, and from tide-neu-07 by featuring a cost-discount survivor package rather than a ⍟-stacking reclaim engine.",
      "description": "Tide-neu-11 is an almost entirely character-based (28 of 30 cards) abandon-and-dissolve deck whose twin anchors define two interlocking lines of play. Kindred Sparks (4-cost, 2x) collapses to a single ● whenever another survivor is in play, enabling an energy-efficient survivor chain, while Avatar of Cosmic Reckoning (3-cost, 2x) produces an ethereal figment immediately on entering play and harvests 1⍟ each time any ally is dissolved. The core loop uses abandon-for-energy enablers — Nightmare Manifest, Exiles of the Last Light, and Infernal Ascendant all convert abandoned characters directly into ● — to accelerate into higher-cost threats or fund reclaim activations like Stolen Genesis (abandon a character, materialize a higher-cost character from the deck). Dissolution triggers then cash out the board state: Volcanic Channeler refunds ● per dissolved ally, Soulreaver and Scuttled Fortune convert dissolutions into card draw, Dustborn Veteran and Shadowcaller replace dissolved survivors with figment tokens, and Cinderheart grows in ✦ with each abandon and pays ⍟ on its own dissolution. Compared to the nearest sibling (tide-fac-24), which runs a dedicated survivor-subtype recursion loop using Tidewreck Navigator, Graywatch, and Duskwall Delver to cycle survivors out of the void repeatedly, this tide instead spends its abandon outlets on raw energy generation and ⍟ harvesting, treating abandonment as a resource-production act rather than a graveyard-management one; compared to tide-neu-07, which stacks ⍟ through multiple passive dissolution watchers (2x Silent Avenger, 2x Skull Weaver) and leans on Titan of Forgotten Echoes for a reclaim/void-loop finish, this tide's signature plays are the low-cost survivor discount and the Avatar's immediate figment production, making it faster to establish a board presence and less reliant on building a deep ⍟ pool.",
      "color": "purple",
      "claims": {"mechanics": ["abandon","figment"]},
      "role": "neutral",
      "leanCardId": "fbf725ca-8837-46d4-970c-922153e27b6e",
      "cards": [
        {"id":"a30a5fdc-a6ec-4289-89cf-40f5cbe6fbaa","name":"Kindred Sparks","subtype":"Survivor","text":"If you control a survivor, you may play this card from your hand or void for 1●.","copies":2},
        {"id":"cbabe603-1333-42bd-85c0-555c664b60b3","name":"Silent Mourner","subtype":"Ancient","text":"▸Materialized: Materialize a 1✦ ethereal figment.\n\nWhen a character you control is dissolved, gain 1⍟.","copies":2},
        {"id":"0458658d-7e02-4286-9249-93674d16620b","name":"Iron Pharaoh","subtype":"Ancient","text":"▸Dawn: Gain 1●.\n\n☾, Abandon a character: Gain 1●.","copies":1},
        {"id":"123baf70-305a-4583-bdba-a10b5153fbeb","name":"Dustborn Veteran","subtype":"Survivor","text":"When a non-figment survivor you control is dissolved, materialize a 1✦ survivor figment.","copies":1},
