    {
      "id": "tide-neu-12",
      "name": "Broad: Starlight Guide / Sworn Defender",
      "shortName": "Warrior Removal Tempo",
      "displayName": "The Sundering Vanguard",
      "displayDescription": "Grinds out wins with enemy banishment and power that scales with its Warrior army.",
      "summary": "A broad warrior tribal deck that leverages enemy banishment and warrior-count spark scaling to grind out wins, distinguishing itself from its sibling tides by packing multiple removal tools rather than relying on abandon-for-resource or dissolved-warrior recursion engines.",
      "description": "Tide-neu-12 is a character-heavy deck (26 of 30 cards are characters) built around maintaining a wide warrior board and converting that board presence into +✦ through several interlocking lords: Skyflame Commander grants supported characters +1✦ for each allied warrior, Assault Leader pumps every warrior at dawn, Company Commander scales when any warrior is played, and Shadow Reflection converts warrior count into a burst of spark on a single challenger. What sets this tide apart from its nearest siblings — tide-neu-04 and tide-fac-29 — is its emphasis on enemy removal rather than warrior recycling: Bladefall (fast/interrupt, banish an enemy), Shattering Gambit (banish at the cost of opponent gaining 5⍟), Glimmerwood Scout (banish a ≤4● enemy on materialization), Gatebound Warden (temporary banish on challenge), and Ambush Operative (fast Offering with an enter-the-battlefield banish) collectively give the deck an unusually deep suite of interaction. Where tide-neu-04 and tide-fac-29 win by abandoning warriors to generate energy or dissolved recursion chains through cards like Burning Revenant and Cinderblade Legionnaire, tide-neu-12 instead keeps its warriors alive longer by clearing threats, then closes with high-spark finishers such as Revered Prince (cost reduced per ally) and Assault Trooper (X-cost and X-spark). Supporting pieces like Epiphany Unfolded (draw 3, fast/interrupt), Reforged Automaton (draw a warrior on materialization), and Wasteland Holdout (figment triggers → ⧗ → card draw) provide the card flow needed to sustain that aggressive removal-backed board plan.",
      "color": "yellow",
      "claims": {"tribe": "Warrior"},
      "role": "neutral",
      "leanCardId": "f3282494-2fcf-4c06-bfbe-3474b28aa87a",
      "cards": [
